# ASID over USB-MIDI: ALGORITHM (KNOB 2 in SONGS) picks the output; ASID only is silent here
# (the emulation still runs, for the scopes), SID + ASID is not; a pause sends the volume at 0 and 0x4D, at which the receiver here resets its chips (as
# the SidStation and TherapSID do), so a resume must send every register again;
# a new song (SELECT: it waits for PLAY) sends the chip type, and on PLAY the whole image
# again. The stream is kept in asid.bin.
# Commando (@SID1@) never gates a voice off and on within one play call, so no message of it
# may hold a control register twice: that would be two frames merged into one message.
sid @SID1@ 50
sid @SID2@ 50
asid asid.bin
expect output 0
turn K2 1
expect output 1
tap PLAY
wait 1000
expect playing 1
expect asid_starts 1
expect asid_types 1
expect asid_msgs >30
expect asid_bad 0
peakreset
mark
wait 500
expect peak_db_max -100
expect dscope >20000
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
expect asid_stops 1
expect asid_vol_at_stop 0
expect asid_double 0
# a knob turned while paused reaches neither the receiver nor the volume
tap SEL
turn K1 3
wait 100
expect asid_seen0 0
turn ALGO 1
expect output 2
tap PLAY
wait 60
expect asid_seen0 25
wait 1000
expect peak_db_min -40
tap PLAY
expect asid_stops 2
expect asid_vol_at_stop 0
turn SELECT 1
wait 1500
expect cur 1
expect playing 0
expect asid_types 2
tap PLAY
wait 60
expect playing 1
expect asid_seen0 25
tap PLAY
expect asid_vol_at_stop 0
turn ALGO 1
expect output 0
expect asid_stops >2
expect asid_bad 0
